# oracle: native binary restart (serial file, b332f28 write_restart) of pair_style hybrid/overlay (pair_hybrid.cpp write_restart: the sub-style keywords and settings only; pair_coeff is re-issued); the 108-atom lj melt (50 steps) is written natively with that pair style, then read and continued for 100 steps
# oracle-inputs: w185nr_hybrid_overlay.restart
# native: b332f28 built as the parity binary wrote w185nr_hybrid_overlay.restart (atom_style charge, charges +-0.4)
read_restart    w185nr_hybrid_overlay.restart
pair_coeff 1 1 lj/cut 1.0 1.0
pair_coeff 2 2 lj/cut 0.8 0.9
pair_coeff * * coul/cut
neighbor        0.3 bin
thermo_style    custom step temp epair emol etotal press
thermo_modify   format float %.15g
thermo          50
fix             1 all nve
run             100
# oracle-compare: thermo=all atoms=all rel=1e-9 abs=1e-12
# measured: max relative error 5.8e-15 (native restart continuation, engine vs native thermo and per-atom), so the tolerance is 1e-9
